[ti:A Perfect Alibi]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:11.31]What was wrong with the man's story? | 那个人的说法有什么破绽？
[00:16.13]'At the time the murder was committed, I was travelling on the 8 o'clock train to London,' said the man. | “凶案发生时，我正坐在开往伦敦的8点钟的火车上，”那个人说。
[00:25.96]'Do you always catch such an early train?' asked the inspector. | “您总是赶这样早的火车吗？”探长问。
[00:31.71]'Of course I do,' answered the man. | “当然，”那人回答说。
[00:35.86]'I must be at work at 10 o'clock. | “我10点钟必须上班。
[00:39.00]My employer will confirm that I was there on time.' | 我的雇主会证明我是准时到的。”
[00:44.69]'Would a later train get you to work on time?' asked the inspector. | “晚一点的火车也能让您准时上班吗？”探长问。
[00:51.08]'I suppose it would, but I never catch a later train.' | “我想可以的，但我从来不赶晚一点的火车。”
[00:57.15]'At what time did you arrive at the station?' | “您几点钟到的火车站？”
[01:02.05]'At ten to eight. I bought a paper and waited for the train.' | “7点50分。我买了张报纸，一直在等车。”
[01:08.08]'And you didn't notice anything unusual?' | “您没有注意到什么异常情况吗？”
[01:13.13]'Of course not.' | “当然没有。”
[01:15.68]'I suggest,' said the inspector,' that you are not telling the truth. | “我提醒您，”探长说，“您说的不是实话。
[01:22.98]I suggest that you did not catch the 8 o'clock train, | 我提醒您，您乘的不是8点钟的火车，
[01:27.84]but that you caught the 8.25 which would still get you to work on time. | 而是8点25分的班车，它同样能让您按时上班。
[01:34.87]You see, on the morning of the murder, the 8 o'clock train did not run at all. | 要知道，凶案发生的那天早晨，8点钟的火车根本没有开。
[01:42.66]It broke down at Ferngreen station and was taken off the line.' | 它在芬格林车站出了故障，被调离了运行线路。”
